# Firebase
.firebase/
firebase.exe
# NEW (CTO mandate — Erode Offers pipeline fix, extended for the PWA
# update-flow fix): firestore.rules AND firebase.json were both
# gitignored, so a fix could exist locally and never actually be
# deployed with no way to tell from the repo — this exact pattern
# caused THREE separate recurrences: undeployed erode_offers rule,
# undeployed erode_offers composite index, and now firebase.json
# itself (which carries the Cache-Control headers fixing the PWA
# "Update button claims success but doesn't refresh" bug) being
# invisible to git. Tracking both now so hosting/rules/index config
# changes are visible in git history and diffs going forward — no more
# silent "it's fixed on my machine" drift.

# 🚨 CRITICAL: Service account key - NEVER commit this file
/backend-admin/serviceAccountKey.json
/scripts/serviceAccountKey.json

# 🔐 Signing: keystore credentials — NEVER commit
/android/key.properties

# Local temporary files
*_output.txt
*.txt
*.exe

# 🔐 Environment variables (API keys, secrets) — NEVER commit
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Claude Code local preview/launch tooling — machine-specific, not for commit
.claude/

# Working-note/review diffs generated during Claude-assisted sessions —
# scratch artifacts for human review, not project source
plans/*.diff
plans/*.new

# Android signing keys. NEVER commit these.
# The release key lives in the ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 GitHub secret
# and is written to android/app/ only inside CI. A copy sitting in the
# working tree (admin-release.jks was created at the repo root on
# Sep 4 2026) is one `git add -A` away from being in the history
# forever, and a leaked signing key cannot be rotated without breaking
# every already-installed app's update path.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
key.properties
